    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d139">

                <pb facs="0145" n="133" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg133"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to the British Prime Minister</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Churchill</hi>)<anchor n="13" xml:id="d139-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-08-26">26 August 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>608. Personal for the Former Naval Person. Your 755<anchor n="14"
                        xml:id="d139-f2"/> and 770.<anchor n="15" xml:id="d139-f3"/> I have no
                    objection to your making preparations to have in <pb facs="0146" n="134"
                        xml:id="pg134"/> readiness a sufficient British Force to preserve order in
                    Greece when the German Forces evacuate that country. There is also no objection
                    to the use by General Wilson of American transport airplanes that are available
                    to him at that time and that can be spared from his other operations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Roosevelt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
